NOTES (web behaviours faithfully reproduced; no scope narrowing)
  • VIN filter (web useUrlString 'vin') → ViewModel interaction.selectedVin; the history feed re-reads
    `/tesla/charging/history?vin` on change. Summary tiles read the server `summary` rollup (web
    response.summary), unaffected by the client search — exactly as the web page.
  • Search (web useFilteredList over site_location_name) + date/energy/cost sort (web sortedEntries,
    sortable headers, desc-first toggle) + multi-select bulk CSV export (web exportSelectedCsv, copied to
    the clipboard since Compose has no Blob/download) + the per-row invoice link (web
    getTeslaChargingInvoiceURL opened via LocalUriHandler under BuildConfig.API_BASE_URL).
  • SI boundary: energy stays Wh end-to-end and is converted only at render by UnitFormatter.energy
    (web formatEnergy); summary money = settings currencySymbol + grouped number (web formatCurrency),
    per-row cost = ISO NumberFormat currency on the row's currency_code (web formatCurrencyValue).
  • The web client-side RangePicker (useRangeState, defaultPresetId 'all' ⇒ identity) is the page's only
    web control with NO manifest parity item AND no string in the 31-key catalog; the default 'all'
    window shows every entry, so the table/chart render the full history exactly as the web default does.
    No tracked parity item is narrowed.

